\par\par \b \uc2  Norway has no plans to contact ECB on euro-Restad. \b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OSLO, May 6 (Reuters) - Norwegian Finance Minister Gudmund Restad said on Wednesday Norway had no plan to contact the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for possible cooperation on monetary policy after the launch of the euro from 1999. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there is a special reason for contact. They know what we will do," Restad told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  Restad announced earlier that Norway would extend its policy of keeping the crown stable against foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the euro supplants the Ecu from 1999. The Ecu is the current anchor of Norway's crown. \par \par \uc2  Restad also said there were no plans to seek a bilateral deal with the ECB on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  variations. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1990 pegged the crown to the Ecu and set up swap accords with European central banks in a strategy of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  variations. \par \par \uc2  That deal collapsed in 1992 just before Norway abandoned the formal link with the Ecu. \par \par \uc2  ((Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41, fax +47 22 42 00 18, oslo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5605vff\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
