\par\par \b \uc2  Norway fin min says stable crown helps wage talks. \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OSLO, Dec 5 (Reuters) - Finance Minister Gudmund Restad on Friday reaffirmed Norway's monetary policy goal of keeping the crown stable on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, saying it was an important tool to help keep a lid on wage rises. \par \par \uc2  "It is the government's target to stick to it (a stable crown). It is also an important condition among other things for wage negotiations," he told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "If the condition of a stable crown is removed, I think it would be much harder to get agreement on a moderate wage round," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said that keeping wages in check at a time of strong economic growth by the oil-backed economy would be one of his biggest challenges in coming months. \par \par \uc2  Restad rejected suggestions by some economists that Norway should switch monetary policy to a goal of keeping inflation in check, away from the existing target of keeping the crown stable against a basket of European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He declined to say how big a swing was possible for the crown against a basket of European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  under current guidelines. \par \par \uc2  Last month \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to keep the crown stable against the Ecu, urged greater flexibility in Norway's monetary policy, saying that it wanted to allow greater swings for the crown. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry replied at the time that current guidelines allowed sufficient "flexibility". \par \par \uc2  Restad said that: "If there are situations with especially strong pressures on the crown in either direction, the crown rate can change in the short term, but the bank will use instruments so that the rate is brought back to the original range after a while." \par \par \uc2  ((Alister Doyle, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41, fax +47 22 42 00 18, oslo.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc501d86\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
