\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2  C.Bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  to stabilise crown. \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OSLO, Oct 9 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Norges Bank, said on Thursday it been selling crowns on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during the second half of September in order to stabilise the petrocurrency. \par \par \uc2  Norges Bank is often seen buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of its role to manage the state's Petroleum Fund. \par \par \uc2  "We have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  outside of the Petroleum Fund (acquisitons) since the second half of September," Leif Eide, a director at the bank, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it had sold 1.264 billion crowns between Wednesday and Friday last week. To date this year it has sold a net 55.932 billion crowns, it said. \par \par \uc2  As well as its role in managing the Petroleum Fund, Norges Bank also has the mandate from the government to use monetary policy to maintain a stable exchange rate of the crown against a basket of European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has appreciated strongly since mid-September, climbing around two percent against the inverse European \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Unit (ECU) index and the mark, to which it touched around 3.98. \par \par \uc2  The crown has weakened slightly since last week and at 1300 GMT it stood at 99.22 versus the ECU index and at 4.0420 compared with the mark. \par \par \uc2  Eide said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was due to the strength of the crown and short-term developments of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The crown was not very stable and there were large swings during the day. Our \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was to try and stabilise it," he said. \par \par \uc2  John Eriksen, analyst at I.D.E.A. in London, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was uneasy about the crown's rapid appreciation, although this was not surprising given its goal of monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  "If the crown continues to strengthen we cannot rule out rate cuts despite the hot economy," Eriksen said. "But at the moment there doesn't seem to be a dramatic situation." \par \par \uc2  --Tanya Pang, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dta901fqt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
