\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Norway crown firms on fixed deposit rate. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tanya Pang \par \uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OSLO, June 16 (Reuter) - The Norwegian crown bounced back from early lows on Thursday after Norway's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Norges Bank, announced it had set an interest rate of 3.6 percent for its fixed-term deposit rate for the period July 1 to July 14. \par \par \uc2  Norges Bank regularly announces fixed-term deposits or fixed-term loans, which usually are carried out through ordinary auction, in order to control money market liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the bank appeared to be testing the market's reaction to higher money market rates to see if it was enough to stabilise the crown. \par \par \uc2  "It is a clear signal that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is uncomfortable with the situation of low interest rates and a weak crown and they want to put up money market rates," said an Oslo-based economist. \par \par \uc2  The crown pulled back to around the 4.1990 level against the mark immediately after the announcement from above 4.21. At 1200 GMT, it stood at 4.1970. \par \par \uc2  The bank has previously announced fixed interest rates at times of instability in the money market or if the fixed term collided with a repo arrangement, Leif Eide, department head at the bank said. \par \par \uc2  Eide said the bank's announcement was an attempt to carefully bring money market rates closer to the comparable ECU rates. \par \par \uc2  In the last auction between June 25 and July 1, the average fixed-term deposit rate was 3.46 percent and the highest rate was 3.52 percent. \par \par \uc2  At 1124 GMT, Norway's three-month money market rate stood at 3.59 percent, while the comparable ECU rate was 4.14 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Following the pressure against the crown half a year ago, we reduced official interest rates almost down to German levels," Eide told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "Now the crown is more or less normalised, but interest rates are still considerably lower than ECU interest rates." \par \par \uc2  One London-based player said the move to a fixed rate could indicate a potential rise in official interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "This could be the first warning shot of a hike in official rates. The bank is concerned about the weak crown. It already has announced that it will begin \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to try and stabilise it. Now maybe they are giving an initial milder signal to the market. The potential threat is there," he said. \par \par \uc2  On June 17 Norges Bank lifted a self-imposed ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in order to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Norway uses monetary policy to stabilise the crown and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain a level that is not officially declared. \par \par \uc2  In January the bank announced it would stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  after three interest rate cuts in two months and extensive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to dampen a surge in the crown. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official deposit rate is 3.25 percent and the overnight lending rate is 5.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  --Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6q03g68\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
