\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Norway  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  returns to  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tanya Pang \par \uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OSLO, June 17 (Reuter) - Norway's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday lifted a self-imposed ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in order to stabilise the crown. \par \par \uc2  The bank said it had decided to reverse a decision in January not to step into the currrency market following a recent slide in the crown. Any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be limited, however, it said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses monetary policy to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain a level that is not officially declared. \par \par \uc2  But on January 10 the bank, Norges Bank, announced it would stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  after three interest rate cuts in two months and extensive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to dampen a surge in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The bank, however, has continued to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to service Norway's huge Petroleum Fund, into which the budget surplus is pumped every year for investment abroad. \par \par \uc2  "Norges Bank's transactions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market have since January 10 1997 been confined to regular purchases of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the equivalent of about NOK 3 billion per month for the Government Petroleum Fund," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  "In the light of developments in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Norges Bank no longer finds it appropriate to maintain special limitations on the use of instruments for the purpose of exchange rate management," it said. \par \par \uc2  "This means we are lifting the self-imposed decision not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Leif Eide, executive director of monetary policy at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "We don't see any strong pressure any more on the crown to appreciate," he added. \par \par \uc2  Recently the crown has weakened considerably, losing around two percent since June 3. \par \par \uc2  Market players attributed the fall to higher-than-expected inflation figures for May, weaker oil prices and growing concern over the outcome of parliamentary elections in September, based on recent opinion polls. \par \par \uc2  The thin Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market means movements are often exaggerated in little volume. \par \par \uc2  The crown immediately rose on Tuesday as market players took the bank's announcement as a signal that the situation had normalised and that it wanted to stabilise the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  At 0910 GMT it stood at 103.07 against the inverse European \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Unit index and at 4.1930 against the mark, compared with 103.95 and 4.2310, respectively, at 0630 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Harald Andreassen, chief economist at Oslo-based Elcon Securities, said the bank's decision was sensible given recent strong fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  "It's better to use \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  than interest rates to stabilise short-term swings in the market. This is a very sensible solution," Andreassen said, adding that he saw little chance of the bank raising interest rates in the near future. \par \par \uc2  "In order for them to do that (raise interest rates) what they are doing today wouldn't work, but we already see that it is working," he said. \par \par \uc2  Stein Bruun, senior analyst at Orkla Finans, said the bank had sent a calming signal to both \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets. But it was too early to tell if the crown's recent fall was a fundamental shift in the exchange level. \par \par \uc2  "The pace and the size of the weakening has been concerning but I think this was caused by a few sellers and a breaking of several technical levels. Foreigners are concerned about inflation and there's growing concern that the situation in parliament will be messy after the election. \par \par \uc2  "But on the other hand you have one of the best economies, there are not many countries with a budget surplus of six percent (of gross domestic product) and a current account of seven percent," Bruun said. \par \par \uc2  --Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6h03zf1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
