\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2  c.bank lifts self-imposed  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  curb. \b0\par\par\uc2 276 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OSLO, June 17 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced on Tuesday it no longer finds it necessary to maintain some self-imposed limits on its management of the crown exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  It said developments in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, where the crown has weakened recently, facilitated such a move. \par \par \uc2  The bank on January 10 gave up trying to stop the crown from appreciating and said it would let the petrocurrency run its course for a while. \par \par \uc2  "Norges Bank's transactions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market have since January 10, 1997 been confined to regular purchases of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the equivalent of about NOK 3 billion per month for the Government Petroleum Fund," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  "In the light of developments in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Norges Bank no longer finds it appropriate to maintain special limitations on the use of instruments for the purpose of exchange rate management," it said. \par \par \uc2  "Any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will normally be undertaken with a view to curbing short-term fluctuations in the value of the Norwegian crown and will thus be on a limited scale," it said. \par \par \uc2  "This means we are lifting the self-imposed decision not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Leif Eide, executive director of monetary policy at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "We don't see any strong pressure any more on the crown to appreciate," he added. \par \par \uc2  The crown stood at 4.2020 against the German mark at 0725 GMT, compared with 4.2125 against the mark at 1400 GMT on Monday. \par \par \uc2  --Rolf Soderlind, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6h03zag\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
