\par\par \b \uc2  Norway  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2:To Curb Short-Term Kr Fluctuations \b0\par\par\uc2 155 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1997\par 09:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (AP-Dow Jones)--Norges Bank, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Tuesday it will resume \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb short-term fluctuations in the value of the Norwegian krone. \par \par \uc2  Since Jan. 10, Norges Bank's transactions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market have been confined to regular purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the equivalent 3 billion kroner per month for the State Petroleum Fund. \par \par \uc2  According to a written statement, the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  no longer finds it 'appropriate to maintain special limitations on the use of instruments for the purpose of exchange rate management' in the light of recent developments in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Since late February the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened by over 5% against the Deutsche mark, and at 0724 GMT the mark was quoted at 4.2035 kroner. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0736GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6h04dvv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
