\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Norway's Krone Muscles Higher Against DM \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1997\par 17:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM (AP-Dow Jones)--The remarkable rally in the Norwegian krone which forced the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut its key rate twice in a week, continued Monday and late in the session the German mark had slipped close to 4.000 kronor. \par \par \uc2  At 1545 GMT the Deutsche mark changed hands at 4.0050 kroner, down from 4.0200 kronor in early morning trade, and markedly lower from 4.0370 kronor late Friday in Europe. \par \par \uc2  Traders accredited some of the strength to a generally weaker German mark but said that most of Monday's gains came in the wake of statements about interest rates and monetary policy over the weekend by Norway's finance minister, Jens Stoltenberg. \par \par \uc2  'The finance minister's comments added to last week's rally and the stronger it gets the more players seem to want to hop on the train,' said a trader at a major Scandinavian bank. \par \par \uc2  In an article in Oslo newspaper Aftenposten Stoltenberg said that 'there is room lower interest rates in Norway.' \par \par \uc2  Stoltenberg also said in Aftenposten that Norges Bank's decision Friday to step down its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market won't change \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main and only monetary policy goal of a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The comments followed a busy week in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, where Norges Bank cut key interest rates twice last week in an effort to stem the Norwegian krone's rapid appreciation. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key deposit rate now stands at 3.25% and the overnight lending at 5.25% \par \par \uc2  In the near term traders are taking a positive view on the krone but caution that the 4.000 kroner level presents a technical resistance level of some dignity. \par \par \uc2  'On top of that, in situations like this, not much is needed to provoke a wave of profit taking,' said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-01-97 \par \par \uc2  1605GMT \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1d00dll\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
