\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 :Norway's Krone Up Vs DM; Firmer Trend Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1997\par 13:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Norwegian krone is continuing its appreciation against the Deutsche mark amid moderate buying interest around midday Monday in Europe. \par \par \uc2  Traders say statements about interest rates and monetary policy over the weekend by Norway's finance minister, Jens Stoltenberg, has bolstered interest in the the Norwegian unit. \par \par \uc2  At 1130 GMT the Deutsche mark changed hands at 4.0040 kroner, down from 4.0200 kroner in early morning trade, and markedly lower from 4.0370 kroner late Friday in Europe. \par \par \uc2  'Stoltenberg's comments boosted confidence in the krone, and didn't dampen interest for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said one trader with a Scandinavian bank in Oslo. \par \par \uc2  In weekend article in Aftenposten, an Oslo newspaper, Stoltenberg said, 'There's room lower interest rates in Norway.' \par \par \uc2  'We'll achieve international credibility by maintaining a tight fiscal policy, and showing that we have no intention of fueling the economy with oil funds,' Stoltenberg said in the newspaper interview. \par \par \uc2  Stoltenberg also said in Aftenposten that Norges Bank's decision Friday to step down its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market won't change \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main and only monetary policy goal of a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The comments follow a busy week in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, where Norges Bank cut key interest rates twice last week in an effort to stem the Norwegian krone's rapid appreciation. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key deposit rate now stands at 3.25% and the overnight lending at 5.25% \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, although traders predict the krone will continue to have a strong undertone, the Norwegian unit will encounter resistance at the technically significant 4.0000 kroner a mark level in the near term. Also, profit taking may knock the krone temporarily weaker against the mark, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-01-97 \par \par \uc2  1215GMT \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1d00chp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
