\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2  bank cuts rates again, curbs  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Rolf Soderlind \par \uc2 559 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 1997\par 18:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OSLO, Jan 10 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , facing a runaway crown, cut official interest rates for the second time in two days on Friday only to see the oil-backed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  power to new peaks. \par \par \uc2  The beleaguered bank, buckling under market pressure, simultaneously announced it would now curb its massive but fruitless \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and let the crown run its course for a while. \par \par \uc2  Effective immediately, the bank reduced the deposit rate and the overnight lending rate charged to commercial and savings banks by 25 basis points to 3.25 and 5.25 percent respectively. \par \par \uc2  But markets had discounted the cut, according to dealers. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the crown is undervalued as the Norwegian economy is booming with huge surpluses in the national budget and current account. Norway is the world's second biggest oil exporter after Saudi Arabia. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Jens Stoltenberg said the government had no plans to change \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies despite failing to keep the strong crown from appreciating. \par \par \uc2  "We have not planned for that," Stoltenberg told reporters in response to a question. \par \par \uc2  He said the goal was to gradually return the crown to normal levels, but declined to say how this might be done. "I don't want to say anything about possible measures. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the operative responsibility. It is the job of a finance minister to be a bit unclear in some areas." \par \par \uc2  The bank on Wednesday announced a 50 basis point reduction in both rates effective Thursday, but in vain. Friday's cut also failed to slow down the crown's bull run. \par \par \uc2  "The crown exchange rate has recently been under persistent pressure," the bank said in a statement. "Norges Bank (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) has purchased foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  equivalent to 20 billion Norwegian crowns ($3.13 billion) since the start of 1997." \par \par \uc2  The primary objective of Norwegian monetary policy is exchange rate stability. The crown is in a dirty float, which means the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain a level that is not officially declared. \par \par \uc2  Announcing a temporary policy shift, the bank said "...in the light of developments in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Norges Bank will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to any substantial extent in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over a period". \par \par \uc2  Oystein Stephansen at S-E Banken in Oslo, commenting on the bank's decision to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told Reuters Financial Television (RFTV): \par \par \uc2  "It means that the crown might be more volatile than we've seen before, that the markets are going to have a closer look at the crown, possibly test it towards the D-mark...We are going to see a new level for the crown. \par \par \uc2  "I expect it to stay there at least in the short term. We would have to see whether economic fundamentals then justify that level or whether we still have what you call an undervalued crown," Stephansen said. \par \par \uc2  The mark plunged to its lowest level against the Norwegian crown for more than four years because of a combination of weak German economic data released on Thursday and the curbing of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The mark/Norwegian crown rate fell to a low of 4.03 per mark before recovering to 4.0470/10 by midsession. At the start of this week the crown stood around 4.13 per mark. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt1a07wld\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
