\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  gains to stay in spotlight. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Abigail Schmelz \par \uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 1997\par 17:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM, Jan 10 (Reuter) - Nordic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly the Norwegian crown, are expected to continue feeling upward pressure after lively \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Friday ranging from market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to high-speed key rate cuts, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , facing a runaway crown, cut official interest rates for the second time in two days on Friday only to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  power more than two percent in three days to a new four-year peak of 4.03 per mark at one stage. \par \par \uc2  Buckling under market pressure, the bank simultaneously announced it would now curb its massive but fruitless \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and let the crown run its course for a while. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Finland, Denmark and Sweden said their central banks had also sold their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , all of which have also been strengthening recently, for German marks. \par \par \uc2  The Norwegian and Swedish crowns have each risen more than two percent since January 7. The Danish crown and Finnish markka rises have been notable though less dramatic. \par \par \uc2  Dollar strength, coupled with strong economic growth prospects, have boosted \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the Nordic area although only Norway has so far seen the market test levels significant enough to force key rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  Oystein Stephansen at S-E Banken in Oslo told Reuters Financial Television the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would lead to more volatility. \par \par \uc2  "Markets are going to have a closer look at the crown, possibly test it towards the D-mark. It is a tough call today when the markets are moving very rapidly. We are going to see a new level for the crown," he said. \par \par \uc2  Sweden's Riksbank, eager to show the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is stable without being linked to the European Union's Exchange Rate Mechansim (ERM), has already said it would enter the market to iron out sudden crown movements. \par \par \uc2  "It is a small stake to stop the strengthening of the crown in the international turbulence," one dealer said. "The Riksbank is not worried about the crown in itself." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's recent surge has sparked interest in peripheral \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly in the Nordic ones because their economies have stronger than average European growth prospects. \par \par \uc2  Swedish economic think-tank KI forecasts gross domestic product (GDP) growth of 2.7 percent in 1997. Official forecasts for Finland are for GDP growth of up to four percent in 1997. \par \par \uc2  The Norwegian government said in its budget it expected 1997 GDP growth of 3.1 percent for the overall economy and 2.5 percent excluding oil production. For Denmark, consensus market forecasts are for 1997 GDP of 2.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said these strong fundamentals suggest further gains for the Finnish markka, which has been linked to Europe's ERM since last October. \par \par \uc2  "On balance, there are strengthening pressures on the markka," SE-Banken's Helsinki chief economist Esko Torsti said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt1a07wib\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\