\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : NOK Softer Vs DEM; After Early Firming Bout \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 1996\par 14:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Norwegian krone is slightly softer against the Deutsche mark early Thursday afternoon in Europe, after a firming bout by the Norwegian unit earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  Traders say the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold kroner earlier in the European session, in an effort to dampen the krone's strengthening streak. \par \par \uc2  In spot trade at 1310 GMT, the Deutsche mark is fetching 4.1932 kroner, up from 4.1885 in early morning trade Thursday, but little changed from 4.1935 kroner late Wednesday in Europe. \par \par \uc2  According to dealers, Norges Bank, \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market selling kroner at around the 4.1910 kroner a mark level to 4.1920 kroner a mark level earlier in the day for undisclosed amounts. Traders say the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came as a counter-reaction to strong interest in the krone from foreign investors early on. \par \par \uc2  In line with normal practice, Norges Bank refused to comment on any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But traders say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize the krone. \par \par \uc2  According to analysts, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intention isn't to target a specific level for the krone, but rather to dampen too sharp strengthening or weakening movements by the Norwegian unit. \par \par \uc2  However, looking ahead, markets players say the recent firming pressure on the krone will persist as strong economic fundamentals and a strong price of oil continue to underpin the Norwegian unit. \par \par \uc2  A trader with an Oslo-based bank predicted the krone is heading for the significant 101.00 points level on its theoretical ECU index in the near term. At around mid-session in Europe the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was slightly softer at 101.23 points on the ECU index, from 101.21 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-11-96 \par \par \uc2  1314GMT \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsbe00tv5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
