\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 -2: Mkt Mixed On Chances Of Norwegian Rate Cut \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 1996\par 14:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, measured on its theoretical ECU index, which moves inversely to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength, the krone was at 101.28 points at 1320 GMT, slightly weaker compared with 101.15 points late Friday in Europe. \par \par \uc2  In the near term, dealers expect the krone to stick to its current level of around 101.30 index points on its theoretical ECU index. \par \par \uc2  However, looking further ahead, market players are mixed about the chances of new interest rate easing from the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Last week, Norges Bank surprised market players when it slashed 0.5 percentage point off its key rates, bringing its deposit rate to 4.00% and its overnight lending rate to 6.00%. \par \par \uc2  Some traders say the strengthening pressure on the krone will continue, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to test the significant 4.1940 kroner a mark level. This was the level at which \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily last week to stem the krone's strengthening, traders say. \par \par \uc2  However, others argue that profit-taking is bound to set in after the Norwegian unit's recent firming run and this will relieve Norway's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from any immediate need to trim official interest rates in the near term. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Following are exchange rates for Nordic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1351 GMT Monday,\par