\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2 's NOK Gains Slightly Vs. DEM After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 199 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 1995\par 15:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (AP-DJ)--The Norwegian krone (NOK) is slightly stronger against the Deutsche mark shortly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by U.S. and Japanese central banks to strengthen the dollar Wednesday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  The Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it didn't participate in any concerted European \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and Norwegian dealers say they saw no sign of any other European central banks in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  'The market was ripe for an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this time,' said Aamund Lunde, an analyst with Den norske Bank AS in Oslo. 'The dollar had gained against the yen overnight, but it needed a push to make the same gains against the Deutsche mark as well.' \par \par \uc2  He said it was too early to say whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would actually work, but added, 'If it doesn't work, that's a bad omen for the dollar.' \par \par \uc2  At 1350 the mark is trading at 4.4195 kroner, sharply down from 4.4435 kroner late afternoon Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, meanwhile, the Norwegian three-month interbank lending rate (NIBOR) continued to ease Wednesday to 5.53% from 5.55%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-08-95 \par \par \uc2  1349GMT \par \par \uc2  1162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8205ua0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
