\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2  NOK Stable; Minor  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 1995\par 12:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (AP-DJ)--The Norwegian krone remains stable in a tight range in quiet trade Friday, dealers say. \par \par \uc2  They say the krone is trading in the weaker end of its 104.25-104.45 range on the weighted ECU trade index. \par \par \uc2  They say the krone's continuing weak position probably spurred a small \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen the krone in early morning trade Friday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought kroner regularly in the past few weeks in an attempt to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The krone has slipped some on the ECU index since March, when it traded around 103.20 at its strongest. \par \par \uc2  Although the Norwegian krone is officially floating, the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  with small amounts to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, traders say the market is calm ahead of the release of the government's revised budget Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'The numbers aren't out yet, but the trend is widely known,' said a dealer with Den norske Bank AS in Bergen. 'The government is likely to tighten the budget further, and the market loves it.' \par \par \uc2  The budget currently has a deficit of 11 billion kroner, or 1.4% of gross domestic product (GDP). The newspaper Aftenposten reported earlier this week that the government plans to trim several billion kroner from the deficit. but not enough to swing it into a surplus. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts say they expect parliament to pass a budget with a surplus for next year. \par \par \uc2  On the international arena, dealers say they are looking for the French presidential election Sunday to calm European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets some. They say worries ahead of the election have spilled over to other markets, including Scandinavia. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, meanwhile, the three-month interbank lending rate tightened to 5.76% from 5.64%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-05-95 \par \par \uc2  1027GMT \par \par \uc2  1162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr55039vh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
