\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Norway \highlight\uc2 's NOK Weaker;  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  Deemed 'Unsuccessful' \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 1995\par 10:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (AP-DJ)--The Norwegian krone is markedly weaker against the Deutsche mark Thursday morning following the mark's sharp strengthening in the wake of Wednesday afternoon's largely unsuccessful \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by U.S., Japanese and German central banks, traders say. \par \par \uc2  But they add that the mark has retreated some from early morning highs, when it almost touched the all-time high from about a month ago. At its strongest Thursday morning, the mark traded at about 4.5030, compared with the all-time high of 4.5125 kroner reached March 8. \par \par \uc2  Since then, the mark has slid some and is trading at 4.4925 kroner in late morning. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the krone is holding stable against other crosses, traders say, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is nonetheless weaker on the theoretical ECU index because the mark is a heavy component in the weighted index, which moves inversely to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. \par \par \uc2  The krone has weakened beyond the 104.00 level on the index for the first time since its broad gain in early March, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dipped down to about 103.20 on the index as it weakened less against the mark than it strengthened against other crosses. In late morning trade, the krone is at 104.04 index points. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the krone could consolidate at this weaker level for awhile, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Norges Bank, probably would like to see a somewhat weaker krone in its attempts to help support the ailing dollar. But they add that the krone is likely to strengthen in the long term because of Norway's solid fiscal situation. \par \par \uc2  'We still believe the krone could appreciate in the course of the year, and that a strengtening beyond 103.00 ECU index points will cause the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower interest rates in the long term,' said Eirik Larsen, senior analyst at Den norske Bank AS (DnB) in Oslo. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-04-95 \par \par \uc2  0850GMT \par \par \uc2  1162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr4602gjm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
