\par\par \b \uc2  Norway's NOK Stable; Lower Money Market Interest Rates \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 13:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (AP-DJ)--Norway's krone is stable to slightly stronger in a quiet market Monday, traders say. \par \par \uc2  In early afternoon trade, the Deutsche mark trades at 4.4785 kroner, down from 4.4820 kroner late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the krone appears to be strengthening some against other crosses. Measured on the unofficial ECU index, which moves inversely to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength, the krone is at 103.27 index points in the early afternoon, compared with 103.41 points late afternoon Friday. \par \par \uc2  'The krone probably won't strengthen much beyond the 103.20 level on the ECU index Monday,' said Arnstein Gundersen with Christiania Bank AS in Stavanger. \par \par \uc2  Local traders say there are no major data, neither from Norway nor from abroad, expected to have any impact on the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday. \par \par \uc2  The foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of Norges Bank, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Norway, remained unchanged at 145 billion kroner Monday and Tuesday last week, the bank said in its twice-weekly report Monday. \par \par \uc2  The size of the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves is released with a one-week delay on Monday and Thursday every week, indicating any \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the bank. Although \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's krone is officially floating, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  with small amounts to keep the krone stable. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, meanwhile, the three-month interbank lending rate has eased Monday to 5.33% compared with 5.45% Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-03-95 \par \par \uc2  1211GMT \par \par \uc2  1162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3k02077\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
