\par\par \b \uc2  Norway's NOK Strengthens In Calming Mkt; U.S. Jobs Data Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 13:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (AP-DJ)--Norway's krone is strengthening Friday as traders await the release of U.S. jobless data at 1330 GMT for a fresh indication of the U.S. economy and the likely course of the dollar in coming days. \par \par \uc2  Measured on the theoretical weighted ECU index, which moves inversely to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength, the krone is at 103.24, compared with 103.63 late afternoon Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders say Norges Bank, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. But, many believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the krone trading below 103.20 on the index. \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  with small amounts to keep the krone stable. \par \par \uc2  Against the Deutsche mark, the krone has also strengthened Friday. At 1150 GMT the mark trades at 4.4535 kroner, down from 4.4725 late afternoon Thursday. \par \par \uc2  'The market is calmer Friday, but there's a sense this is a lull before the storm,' said a dealer with a bank in Northern Norway. There are rumors in the market that there could be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the dollar later Friday, said the dealer. \par \par \uc2  He said the market largely ignored Norwegian consumer price data released Friday. The state statistics agency said Norwegian prices rose 0.4% in February from January, bringing the year-on-year rise to 2.6%. \par \par \uc2  'Inflation has risen lately, but there's still no fear in the market that the Norwegian economy could be overheating,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Norwegian retail sales data were also released Friday. The state statistics agency said retail sales rose 4.8% in January compared with the same month a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, meanwhile, the three-month interbank lending rate rose Friday to 5.70%, compared with 5.61% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-03-95 \par \par \uc2  1208GMT \par \par \uc2  1162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3a01qm3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
