\par\par \b \uc2  Norway's NOK Weaker Vs DEM; Up From Early Morning Lows \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 13:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (AP-DJ)--The Norwegian krone is weaker versus the Deutsche mark Friday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffers from the latest bout of European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market jitters following concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the dollar Friday morning. \par \par \uc2  At 1200 GMT, the mark is trading at 4.4233 kroner, up from 4.4185 kroner late Thursday in Europe. The krone has regained some strength against the mark though, with the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hitting highs of around 4.4275 kroner early Friday. \par \par \uc2  The krone is however, well above its all-time lows versus the mark which it set earlier this week. On Monday, the mark hit a record high of 4.4405 kroner. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile though, the krone is remaining largely stable on its theoretical European \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Unit (ECU) index, which moves inversely to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. At 1200 GMT, the krone trades at 103.56, compared with 103.52 midday Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Krone traders are keeping their focus on the dollar, with some expecting more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  later Friday. Many see dollar buying by central banks giving a helping hand to the other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the krone in regaining some strength versus the mark. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also participated in Friday morning's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It confirmed that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying dollars two times Friday morning. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, meanwhile, the three-month interbank lending rate eased to 5.26% Friday from 5.32% a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-03-95 \par \par \uc2  1210GMT \par \par \uc2  1162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3301ie0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
