\par\par \b \uc2  Norway's NOK Softer Against DEM, But Strong On ECU Index \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 1995\par 12:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (AP-DJ)--Norway's krone is slipping against the Deutsche mark Friday, but is holding on to its strong gains against other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as market players report the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling off kroner in order to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from firming further. \par \par \uc2  Although the Norwegian krone is officially floating, Norges Bank, \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market with small amounts to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable. \par \par \uc2  Against the Deutsche mark, the krone is weakening in line with most other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In early-afternoon trade Friday the mark is at 4.3908 kroner, up from 4.3865 kroner late afternoon Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But measured on the unofficial weighted ECU index, which moves inverse to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength, the krone is holding on to gains made earlier in the week. The krone is trading at 103.70 point on the index early afternoon Friday, little changed from late Thursday's level of 103.66 points. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say the krone firmed to 103.65 points on the ECU index Friday morning, its strongest level since the krone was allowed to float in 1992. \par \par \uc2  'But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't let the krone strengthen below the 103.70 level,' one dealer said. He said the bank is selling off kroner to offset a further strengthening of the krone against other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now has to make a decision whether its monetary policy should give priority to keeping inflation low or to increasing Norway's competitiveness,' said DnB Fonds, Norway's largest arbitrage company, in an analysis this week. \par \par \uc2  DnB Fonds said a tightening of monetary policies would strengthen the Norwegian krone. Such a policy would enable the bank to fight inflation, but would hurt Norwegian businesses' international competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-02-95 \par \par \uc2  1115GMT \par \par \uc2  1162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr2h013ac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
