\par\par \b \uc2  Norway's NOK Firms; Trade Surplus Rose 54% Mo-On-Mo \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 1995\par 14:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (AP-DJ)--Norway's krone is stronger against most European crosses Monday, notably against a broadly weaker British pound. Dealers said positive trade data released Monday supported the krone's strength. \par \par \uc2  At 1335 GMT the pound trades at 10.3995 kroner, down from 10.4090 kroner late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Measured on the unofficial ECU index, which moves inverse to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength, the krone is at 103.84 points in mid-afternoon trade Monday, compared with 103.90 points late Friday. \par \par \uc2  'The krone is now at its firmest level on the ECU index since November 1992,' said a dealer with Fokus Bank a.s. in Trondheim. \par \par \uc2  He said Norges Bank, the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the krone when it strengthens beyond the 103.85 level on the ECU index. In \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  with small amounts, even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is floating. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said there had been no sign of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market so far Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the Deutsche mark, however, the krone continues to weaken slightly Monday. At 1335 GMT the Deustche mark trades at 4.3796 kroner, up from 4.3753 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trade balance figures released Monday confirmed the krone's strong position. The data, released by the state statistics agency, showed that Norway's trade balance surplus rose 54% to 6.3 billion kroner in January, compared with 4.1 billion kroner a month earlier. \par \par \uc2  Compared with the year earlier, the trade surplus rose 33% from 4.7 billion kroner in January 1994. \par \par \uc2  Excluding the oil and offshore industry, there was a trade deficit in January of 3.6 billion kroner, the same as in January 1994, the statistics agency reported. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, in the money market, the Norwegian three-month interbank lending rate tightened to 5.63% Monday, from 5.47% Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-02-95 \par \par \uc2  1353GMT \par \par \uc2  1162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr2d00wdm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
