\par\par \b \uc2  Norway's NOK Softens In Line With Other Scandinavian Units \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 1995\par 15:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (AP-DJ)--The Norwegian krone is slightly weaker against most European crosses in very light trade mid-afternoon Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Compared with last week, when the Scandinavian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffered a broad softening streak because of turmoil on the international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the krone is firmer this week. But the Norwegain unit is trading within a wider range because of the thin volume. \par \par \uc2  'Last week, the krone moved within the range of 103.94 to 104.05 on the ECU index. Wednesday it has been moving between 103.83 and 104.00,' said a dealer with Handelsbanken in Oslo. The unofficial ECU index moves inversely to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. \par \par \uc2  At 1400 GMT the krone is softer at 104.00 on the index, compared with 103.88 late afternoon Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Although the krone is officially a floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers say in practice the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Norges Bank, will often smooth out ripples in the market with very limited \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tends to sell off small amounts of kroner when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dips below 104.00 on the ECU index. However, \b \highlight22\uc2 Norway\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reports its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  only one week after the event. \par \par \uc2  'In line with the bank's policy, I can't comment on whether we have sold Norwegian kroner in the past few days,' said Leif Eide, director of market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Norway's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Against the Deutsche mark, the krone is softening in line with other Scandinavian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The mark is trading at 4.3777 kroner at 1400 GMT, up from 4.3703 kroner late afternoon Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, the Norwegian three-month interbank lending rate is unchanged from Tuesday at 5.74%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-01-95 \par \par \uc2  1409GMT \par \par \uc2  1162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr1i006pw\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (norway near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum